# Basic instruction: 

### orikawa laurentin
this project is about building my professional portfolio. 
orikawa is founded by me - laurentin rivière - and I brand orikawa as a small hand-crafted brand that designs and sells services of video editing, video production, motion design and graphic design. 
I mainly specialize in digital signal processing industries; implying audio plugins, virtual instruments, saas product and other digital audio related products. 

orikawa is designed to be a small studio, I also plan to collaborate with other freelancers and artists to offer a wider range of services. 

I will be proposing several types of video and products :
- Product trailer-hype video
- Product explainer video
- Product cinematic video
- Brand video
- Website assets
- Motion graphics pack
- film making (event video, corporate video, documentary video)
- Logo animation

Associated with this product, I will also sell audio services like, sound design, musical stinger, related to my activity orion laurentin.

The studio is meant to be specialized onto the dsp industrie and have to insist into the fact that orikawa's founded by a musician and producer
I have the golden rule ; t0v :
- translation : translate complex idea into simple and beautiful images
- 0 : 0-friction, I easily understand audio concepts and technical details
- v : value, rise the perceived value of the product

However, I don't want the website to be too corporate and too "professional" in a bad way, it need to feel human and creative and only specialized in this field. I'll let some space to present other projects non-related to dsp industry. I want this integration to be coherent and fluid.


### orikawa aesthetic

Inspired by plan hand crafted / notebook style.

I want a very interactive website, with micro-interactions. A website that feels alive and responsive to the cursor.

I want the aesthetic to be elegant, clean, creative and minimalist, but also warm and human.
I really love the aesthetic of notebooks, papers, drawings, hand-drawn elements, but also high-quality, professional video and animation, so I want to mix those two elements.
you can use line or grid as background on some elements

color palette (by impoortance order) :
the main colors should be:
- cream white #fff7dd
- midnight bkye #131522
- soft blue  #323A72 
The accent colors should be:
- mint #29E3BE
- mimosa #FFF951
- fushia #E019D7

You can take a look at my images; in img folder for references. I want some of the aesthetic to be extracted from there.
I also made a draft : gemini_draft-orikawa_portfolio_web.tsx with gemini web, there is some good ideas you can take inspiration from. But don't copy-paste, I want it to be original and personalized to me.


Fonts :
Main (logo, title) : garamond
Secoundary (Clarity in motion) : Effra
You can add a thord font, pencil paper written like, use it sparingly.

all fonts i already choose are from adobe, if you can't get those, just let me add them manually.


Tech stack I want :
- tailwind
- typescript
- react
- framer motion
- three js
- GSAP
- Spline (for 3d web design)
- vercel for hosting
- I want a fast website, I want it to be SEO optimized, I want it to be accessible, I want it to be responsive, I want it to be interactive, I want it to be creative, I want it to be minimalist, I want it to be elegant, I want it to be warm, I want it to be human, I want it to be alive.



## Website Structure

1. **Header / Navigation**
    
   - soft opacity appearance Brand logo (orikawa laurentin) with animated waves
   - soft opacity appearance Navigation links (Work / Projects, Services (T0V), About / Sound Lab, Contact)
   - soft opacity appearance Interactive micro-element (e.g. sound toggle or playful interactive toggle)

2. **Hero Section**
   - soft opacity appearance Main tagline: *"Clarity in Motion"* with wow effect, reactive background animation, sound reactive (water physics distorting background)
   - Visual Centerpiece: Interactive element :be creative and i'll do an ear candy sound design associated with it, 
   - Call to action: "Explore Works" & "Get in Touch"

3. **Featured Works (Portfolio Showcase)**
    - As the gemini draft shows, I want something inspired by notebook with tabs. But tabs should be on top of notebook (make placeholder for now)
   - Tab 1 : works in dsp industries 
   - Tab 2 : interactive web assets (make placeholder for now) - sound design proof
   - tav 3 : others (make placeholder for now) - motion graphics 
   - Each case studies / cards with video preview on hover, notebook-style metadata (tags, tools used, client)

4. **Value Proposition / The T0V Formula**
   - pencil written typical projects.
   First call (defining needs & goals)
   Second steps : starting production
   Third steps : Review and correction
   Fourth steps : Delivery
   

6. **About / Studio Philosophy**
   - who founded orikawa, musician/producer roots (lorem ipsum for now)
   - Notebook sketch aesthetics / hand-drawn annotations

7. **Footer / Contact**
   - Direct inquiry form, email, social links
   - Warm sign-off note with the handwritten script font
   - legal mentions
   - website plan


